Yup, you're quite right Mark.  In that case, one would need separate information
about either the animal distribution or the detection probability.  The former
could come from an independent survey - e.g., a shipboard survey going away from
the coast; the latter could come from, e.g., a double-platform (mark-recapture
distance sampling) setup.

Cheers, Len

