In terms of using "species" as a covariate, the answer is "probably"; I have 250+ species x 6 habitats. I was under the impression that I needed sufficient detections per species in each of those habitats in order to satisfy the requirements for distance sampling, perhaps I am wrong? Does using covariates circumvent the restrictions relating to minimum volumes of data?

Thanks very much for your advice.
Kind regards,
Tom

